RESULT:MOVING_TIME_MULTICHANNEL_RATE — For raw terms A_j a^-p_j exp(-m_j t) and B_l a^r_l exp(ell_l t) with squared-source normalization a^-2s, the sharp positive logarithmic-time guarantee is min_jl (R_l m_j-P_j ell_l)/(P_j+R_l), capped by min_j(m_j-P_j/h). A target 0<M<min m_j is admissible iff max_j P_j/(m_j-M)<=min_l R_l/(M+ell_l) and <=h; its lower time endpoint is a witness.
  result · T3 · proven · analytic
